<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch06-functions-limits-continuity" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Functions of Several Variables, Limits, and Continuity</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>A function may take several coordinates as inputs and return a number or a vector. Graphs and level sets help visualize such functions; limits and continuity require estimates that control all nearby inputs. We examine path tests, their limitations, and the hypotheses that make continuity useful.</p>
  </introduction>

